  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final rules are all within acceptable ranges or better, with S1 at the safe end (24-hour reporting of every thermal incident and 48-hour customer notice). S2 keeps per-model results with customers and regulators, not the public, and allows a 12-month remediation window before any sales stop, which benefits Northwind's Hearth 10. S5 sets a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no interim trigger and no sales bar after remediation, which bears on Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9."
